{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FvSBzLar7acqweBwQQFUHK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Circuit review experiments — Universal 112 donor (run 8534a2a6)\n2\t\n3\tReviewer role: circuit. Date: 2026-10-16. Tools: kicad-cli 10.0.7, python3 (stdlib, -I), curl, WebFetch/WebSearch.\n4\t\n5\t## 1. Reproduction of native checks\n6\t- ERC rerun (`rerun/erc_rerun2.json`): `kicad-cli sch erc --format json --severity-all --units mm` on\n7\t  /candidate/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch with KICAD10_* env pointed at /candidate/stock.\n8\t  Result: 5 errors (identical set to packet: 3× power_pin_not_driven, 1× pin_not_connected, 1× pin_to_pin),\n9\t  229 endpoint_off_grid, 2 multiple_net_names, 5 isolated_pin_label, 1 same_local_global_label — all match\n10\t  work/erc/erc.json. Library-availability warnings (lib_symbol_issues / footprint_link_issues /\n11\t  lib_symbol_mismatch) differ in count (603 warnings total vs packet 348) because my ad-hoc\n12\t  KICAD_CONFIG_HOME lacks the harness's generated global library tables; all electrically meaningful\n13\t  categories reproduce exactly.\n14\t- DRC rerun (`rerun/drc_rerun.json`): 13 errors (5 padstack + 5 annular_width + 3 starved_thermal),\n15\t  0 unconnected, 114 parity issues — matches work/drc/drc.json exactly for errors/unconnected/parity.\n16\t\n17\t## 2. ERC error triage (all 5 errors)\n18\t- power_pin_not_driven ×3: #PWR01 GND; A1 pin 8 VMOT on /12V_MR_FUSE; J2 pin 90 12V_IGN on /12V_KEY.\n19\t  Supplies enter via passive connector pins (J1.105/106 → F1 → 12V_MR_FUSE; J1.45 → 12V_KEY); no PWR_FLAG\n20\t  on those nets. Battery/key power genuinely present through the harness; ERC modeling only.\n21\t- pin_not_connected: A1 pin 2 ~FLT (DRV8825 carrier open-drain fault output) left unused — safe.\n22\t- pin_to_pin: J2 pins 40+41 both modeled \"Power output\" named 5V_SENSOR_1 and strapped together —\n23\t  paralleled pins of the same module regulator; benign modeling artifact.\n24\t- same_local_global_label and local \"+5V\" labels (root sheet lines 12563/13475/14687/14707/15087/15127 of\n25\t  Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch): connectivity.json shows a single merged +5V net containing all\n26\t  expected consumers (R1.1, R2.2, U1.1, U2.1/U2.4, J2.81, U20.3, U21.3 …) → no floating sub-net.\n27\t\n28\t## 3. DRC error triage\n29\t- padstack/annular ×5: J1 footprint \"Simon:Molex_112_643330100\" contains five unnumbered thru-hole pads\n30\t  with pad size == drill (4/4 mm and 2.2/2.2 mm) at e.g. (71.95,35.49), (120.0,28.49) — connector mounting\n31\t  peg holes modeled as PTH with zero annular ring instead of NPTH. No net; mechanical only.\n32\t- starved_thermal ×3: GND pads C15.2 (107.85,98.76), U7.4 (101.01,102.68), C14.2 (101.59,104.29) get 1 of\n33\t  2 required zone spokes on F.Cu. Still connected (0 unconnected items); solderability/robustness only.\n34\t\n35\t## 4. CAN2 internal wideband bus termination (scoped question)\n36\tSaved state (verified in Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb and wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch):\n37\t- R36 (175.01,140.67) and R37 (81.62,140.55), both value 120, both `(dnp yes)`; schematic carries an\n38\t  explicit \"n.p.\" annotation next to the terminator cell. Pads land on /CAN2+ and /CAN2-.\n39\t- Bus members (connectivity.json): U20.7/6 and U21.7/6 (TJA1051T/3 transceivers for wideband modules U1,\n40\t  U2), J2.73/74 (Polygonus brain module CAN2), J1.15/11 (harness), D10/D11 NUP2105L ESD, C29/C30/C33/C34\n41\t  47 pF line-to-GND (two per line because the sheet is instantiated twice → ≈94 pF/line + ESD + traces).\n42\t- Brain-module side: fetched FOME-Tech/Polygonus (master). psu.kicad_sch contains U4/U5 MCP2551-I-SN and\n43\t  R9/R10 = 120 Ω, not DNP. Wire trace confirms R10 (207.645,125.095, R_Small pins ±2.54) bridges\n44\t  CANH2 (via 211.455,114.935 → hier label CANH2) to CANL2 (via 211.455,135.255 → CANL2). So with a\n45\t  Polygonus installed, internal CAN2 is single-terminated with 120 Ω.\n46\t- RC estimates: with the module's single 120 Ω: τ_diff ≈ 120 Ω × ~80 pF (two 94 pF line-GND caps in\n47\t  series + transceiver/trace) ≈ 10 ns — fine at 1 Mbit/s.\n48\t  With NO termination anywhere (brain module without on-module terminator, nothing populated on base,\n49\t  no external bus): recessive-state differential resistance is only the paralleled transceiver input\n50\t  bias resistances, TJA1051 R_i(cm) = 15–37 kΩ/pin → R_diff ≈ 2×(15–37k)/3 ≈ 10–25 kΩ; τ ≈ 0.7–1.6 µs\n51\t  against a 2 µs bit at 500 kbit/s (1 µs at 1 Mbit/s) → dominant→recessive edges do not settle in time;\n52\t  communication marginal-to-failing.\n53\t- Atlas compatibility claim (README): https://github.com/mck1117/atlas returns HTTP 404 — Atlas CAN2\n54\t  termination could not be verified.\n55\t\n56\t## 5. Interface/pin-identity spot checks (all pass)\n57\t- TJA1051T-3 symbol pin map 1 TXD / 2 GND / 3 VCC / 4 RXD / 5 VIO / 6 CANL / 7 CANH / 8 S matches NXP\n58\t  device; S tied to GND (normal mode); VCC=+5V, VIO=+3.3V (J2.82 module rail) matching the 3.3 V logic of\n59\t  the f042 wideband modules; 100 nF decoupling on both rails per transceiver.\n60\t- Wideband module symbol: pin 5 CAN_RX (input) ← U20.4/U21.4 RXD (output); pin 6 CAN_TX (output) →\n61\t  U20.1/U21.1 TXD (input). Correct pairing, both channels. SEL straps differ between U1 (SEL_1=GND,\n62\t  SEL_2 float) and U2 (SEL_1 float, SEL_2=+5V) → distinct module IDs.\n63\t- TLE9201SG: symbol pin 2 \"VSO\" tied to +3.3V. Infineon datasheet (via DigiKey HTML datasheet) confirms\n64\t  pin 2 = VSO, supply for the SO output, \"tied to 5V or 3.3V depending on logic level\" — correct. DIS\n65\t  pulled up 10 k to +3.3V (R35/R5) → bridge disabled until MCU drives: safe default. OUT1/OUT2 → J1\n66\t  ETB pins with 10 nF snubbing caps; VS on fused 12 V with 10 µF.\n67\t- DRV8825 carrier A1: VMOT=/12V_MR_FUSE + C2 56 µF bulk; nRESET/nSLEEP (pins 13/14) = +5V; mode pins +\n68\t  nENABLE (pins 9–12) = GND (full step, enabled); STEP/DIR = /LS9,/LS10 with 1 k pullups (R1/R2) and 1 k\n69\t  pulldowns (RN1). Polygonus mcu.kicad_sch shows LS9–LS12 are hierarchical outputs of the MCU sheet\n70\t  (3.3 V push-pull GPIO), so drive levels are 0/3.3 V (> DRV8825 VIH 2.2 V), not the 2.5 V divider that\n71\t  open-drain outputs would produce. VNL5090 adder inputs via RN2/RN4 series 1 k: OK.\n72\t- VR module (vr_module_poly): 74HC02 U5 wired as cross-coupled NOR SR latch (pin4→pin3, pin1→pin5) fed\n73\t  by comparator U7 thresh_low/thresh_high paths; unused gate inputs grounded. Output net drives J2.95,\n74\t  LED D1+R6, J5. Consistent window-comparator trigger.\n75\t- VR Conditioner (MAX9924 U10): BIAS stiffened with populated 1 k/1 k divider to VCC/2 + 1 µF (matches\n76\t  internal VCC/2 bias, no conflict); COUT (pin 7) → /VR1+ → J2.96 with 4.7 k pullup R34. Observed:\n77\t  /CRANK + (J1.59) → R25 → R27 → IN− (U10.2) and /CRANK − → R26 → R28 → IN+ (U10.1), i.e. connector\n78\t  polarity is swapped relative to the MAX9924 typical application; output polarity inverts, normally\n79\t  absorbed by firmware edge selection. No stated requirement to judge against — recorded as observation.\n80\t\n81\t## 6. Sheet alias verification\n82\tsha256(\"VR Conditioner.kicad_sch\") == sha256(\"VR conditioner.kicad_sch\") ==\n83\t377a2691ec878301977100851c40e302b2b7864d88cc27c6c305c03bbf14e15b (byte-identical). Root sheet\n84\t(Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch:21553) references \"VR Conditioner.kicad_sch\"; netlist sheet 4\n85\tresolves to it and all VR-conditioner components (U10, JP1, C23–C25, R25–R34) appear in the netlist.\n86\tResidual hazard: two byte-identical files differing only in case will collide on case-insensitive\n87\tfilesystems and can silently diverge when edited.\n88\t\n89\t## 7. Limitations of these experiments\n90\t- Atlas brain module design unavailable (404) — CAN2 termination with Atlas unverified.\n91\t- No SPICE simulation performed (no models for TJA1051/MAX9924); CAN analysis is analytic RC estimate.\n92\t- Connector current ratings, fuse sizing, thermal and transient qualification not assessed (also\n93\t  excluded by packet scope).\n94\t- Downloaded Polygonus sources are upstream master branch, not necessarily the exact revision the donor\n95\t  targets.\n96\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"480c3efe-ca31-49ae-85c1-8e190ef2ac79","uuid":"a8711e13-25d8-48bb-b83a-ff6921548d19","timestamp":"2026-10-17T00:51:25.681Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/experiments/circuit/notes.md","content":"# Circuit review experiments — Universal 112 donor (run 8534a2a6)\n\nReviewer role: circuit. Date: 2026-10-16. Tools: kicad-cli 10.0.7, python3 (stdlib, -I), curl, WebFetch/WebSearch.\n\n## 1. Reproduction of native checks\n- ERC rerun (`rerun/erc_rerun2.json`): `kicad-cli sch erc --format json --severity-all --units mm` on\n  /candidate/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch with KICAD10_* env pointed at /candidate/stock.\n  Result: 5 errors (identical set to packet: 3× power_pin_not_driven, 1× pin_not_connected, 1× pin_to_pin),\n  229 endpoint_off_grid, 2 multiple_net_names, 5 isolated_pin_label, 1 same_local_global_label — all match\n  work/erc/erc.json. Library-availability warnings (lib_symbol_issues / footprint_link_issues /\n  lib_symbol_mismatch) differ in count (603 warnings total vs packet 348) because my ad-hoc\n  KICAD_CONFIG_HOME lacks the harness's generated global library tables; all electrically meaningful\n  categories reproduce exactly.\n- DRC rerun (`rerun/drc_rerun.json`): 13 errors (5 padstack + 5 annular_width + 3 starved_thermal),\n  0 unconnected, 114 parity issues — matches work/drc/drc.json exactly for errors/unconnected/parity.\n\n## 2. ERC error triage (all 5 errors)\n- power_pin_not_driven ×3: #PWR01 GND; A1 pin 8 VMOT on /12V_MR_FUSE; J2 pin 90 12V_IGN on /12V_KEY.\n  Supplies enter via passive connector pins (J1.105/106 → F1 → 12V_MR_FUSE; J1.45 → 12V_KEY); no PWR_FLAG\n  on those nets. Battery/key power genuinely present through the harness; ERC modeling only.\n- pin_not_connected: A1 pin 2 ~FLT (DRV8825 carrier open-drain fault output) left unused — safe.\n- pin_to_pin: J2 pins 40+41 both modeled \"Power output\" named 5V_SENSOR_1 and strapped together —\n  paralleled pins of the same module regulator; benign modeling artifact.\n- same_local_global_label and local \"+5V\" labels (root sheet lines 12563/13475/14687/14707/15087/15127 of\n  Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch): connectivity.json shows a single merged +5V net containing all\n  expected consumers (R1.1, R2.2, U1.1, U2.1/U2.4, J2.81, U20.3, U21.3 …) → no floating sub-net.\n\n## 3. DRC error triage\n- padstack/annular ×5: J1 footprint \"Simon:Molex_112_643330100\" contains five unnumbered thru-hole pads\n  with pad size == drill (4/4 mm and 2.2/2.2 mm) at e.g. (71.95,35.49), (120.0,28.49) — connector mounting\n  peg holes modeled as PTH with zero annular ring instead of NPTH. No net; mechanical only.\n- starved_thermal ×3: GND pads C15.2 (107.85,98.76), U7.4 (101.01,102.68), C14.2 (101.59,104.29) get 1 of\n  2 required zone spokes on F.Cu. Still connected (0 unconnected items); solderability/robustness only.\n\n## 4. CAN2 internal wideband bus termination (scoped question)\nSaved state (verified in Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb and wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch):\n- R36 (175.01,140.67) and R37 (81.62,140.55), both value 120, both `(dnp yes)`; schematic carries an\n  explicit \"n.p.\" annotation next to the terminator cell. Pads land on /CAN2+ and /CAN2-.\n- Bus members (connectivity.json): U20.7/6 and U21.7/6 (TJA1051T/3 transceivers for wideband modules U1,\n  U2), J2.73/74 (Polygonus brain module CAN2), J1.15/11 (harness), D10/D11 NUP2105L ESD, C29/C30/C33/C34\n  47 pF line-to-GND (two per line because the sheet is instantiated twice → ≈94 pF/line + ESD + traces).\n- Brain-module side: fetched FOME-Tech/Polygonus (master). psu.kicad_sch contains U4/U5 MCP2551-I-SN and\n  R9/R10 = 120 Ω, not DNP. Wire trace confirms R10 (207.645,125.095, R_Small pins ±2.54) bridges\n  CANH2 (via 211.455,114.935 → hier label CANH2) to CANL2 (via 211.455,135.255 → CANL2). So with a\n  Polygonus installed, internal CAN2 is single-terminated with 120 Ω.\n- RC estimates: with the module's single 120 Ω: τ_diff ≈ 120 Ω × ~80 pF (two 94 pF line-GND caps in\n  series + transceiver/trace) ≈ 10 ns — fine at 1 Mbit/s.\n  With NO termination anywhere (brain module without on-module terminator, nothing populated on base,\n  no external bus): recessive-state differential resistance is only the paralleled transceiver input\n  bias resistances, TJA1051 R_i(cm) = 15–37 kΩ/pin → R_diff ≈ 2×(15–37k)/3 ≈ 10–25 kΩ; τ ≈ 0.7–1.6 µs\n  against a 2 µs bit at 500 kbit/s (1 µs at 1 Mbit/s) → dominant→recessive edges do not settle in time;\n  communication marginal-to-failing.\n- Atlas compatibility claim (README): https://github.com/mck1117/atlas returns HTTP 404 — Atlas CAN2\n  termination could not be verified.\n\n## 5. Interface/pin-identity spot checks (all pass)\n- TJA1051T-3 symbol pin map 1 TXD / 2 GND / 3 VCC / 4 RXD / 5 VIO / 6 CANL / 7 CANH / 8 S matches NXP\n  device; S tied to GND (normal mode); VCC=+5V, VIO=+3.3V (J2.82 module rail) matching the 3.3 V logic of\n  the f042 wideband modules; 100 nF decoupling on both rails per transceiver.\n- Wideband module symbol: pin 5 CAN_RX (input) ← U20.4/U21.4 RXD (output); pin 6 CAN_TX (output) →\n  U20.1/U21.1 TXD (input). Correct pairing, both channels. SEL straps differ between U1 (SEL_1=GND,\n  SEL_2 float) and U2 (SEL_1 float, SEL_2=+5V) → distinct module IDs.\n- TLE9201SG: symbol pin 2 \"VSO\" tied to +3.3V. Infineon datasheet (via DigiKey HTML datasheet) confirms\n  pin 2 = VSO, supply for the SO output, \"tied to 5V or 3.3V depending on logic level\" — correct. DIS\n  pulled up 10 k to +3.3V (R35/R5) → bridge disabled until MCU drives: safe default. OUT1/OUT2 → J1\n  ETB pins with 10 nF snubbing caps; VS on fused 12 V with 10 µF.\n- DRV8825 carrier A1: VMOT=/12V_MR_FUSE + C2 56 µF bulk; nRESET/nSLEEP (pins 13/14) = +5V; mode pins +\n  nENABLE (pins 9–12) = GND (full step, enabled); STEP/DIR = /LS9,/LS10 with 1 k pullups (R1/R2) and 1 k\n  pulldowns (RN1). Polygonus mcu.kicad_sch shows LS9–LS12 are hierarchical outputs of the MCU sheet\n  (3.3 V push-pull GPIO), so drive levels are 0/3.3 V (> DRV8825 VIH 2.2 V), not the 2.5 V divider that\n  open-drain outputs would produce. VNL5090 adder inputs via RN2/RN4 series 1 k: OK.\n- VR module (vr_module_poly): 74HC02 U5 wired as cross-coupled NOR SR latch (pin4→pin3, pin1→pin5) fed\n  by comparator U7 thresh_low/thresh_high paths; unused gate inputs grounded. Output net drives J2.95,\n  LED D1+R6, J5. Consistent window-comparator trigger.\n- VR Conditioner (MAX9924 U10): BIAS stiffened with populated 1 k/1 k divider to VCC/2 + 1 µF (matches\n  internal VCC/2 bias, no conflict); COUT (pin 7) → /VR1+ → J2.96 with 4.7 k pullup R34. Observed:\n  /CRANK + (J1.59) → R25 → R27 → IN− (U10.2) and /CRANK − → R26 → R28 → IN+ (U10.1), i.e. connector\n  polarity is swapped relative to the MAX9924 typical application; output polarity inverts, normally\n  absorbed by firmware edge selection. No stated requirement to judge against — recorded as observation.\n\n## 6. Sheet alias verification\nsha256(\"VR Conditioner.kicad_sch\") == sha256(\"VR conditioner.kicad_sch\") ==\n377a2691ec878301977100851c40e302b2b7864d88cc27c6c305c03bbf14e15b (byte-identical). Root sheet\n(Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_sch:21553) references \"VR Conditioner.kicad_sch\"; netlist sheet 4\nresolves to it and all VR-conditioner components (U10, JP1, C23–C25, R25–R34) appear in the netlist.\nResidual hazard: two byte-identical files differing only in case will collide on case-insensitive\nfilesystems and can silently diverge when edited.\n\n## 7. Limitations of these experiments\n- Atlas brain module design unavailable (404) — CAN2 termination with Atlas unverified.\n- No SPICE simulation performed (no models for TJA1051/MAX9924); CAN analysis is analytic RC estimate.\n- Connector current ratings, fuse sizing, thermal and transient qualification not assessed (also\n  excluded by packet scope).\n- Downloaded Polygonus sources are upstream master branch, not necessarily the exact revision the donor\n  targets.\n","numLines":96,"startLine":1,"totalLines":96}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FvSBzLar7acqweBwQQFUHK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
