{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011Cg6txE2f6G8ZhuLFRFHNu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. Here is my summary, followed by the structured decisions.\n\n## Adjudication summary\n\n**Checks (both remain accepted).** I re-verified the full native outputs: ERC reports 353 violations including exactly 5 errors, and DRC reports 142 violations including 13 errors (5 padstack + 5 annular width + 3 starved thermal) plus 114 parity issues. Both executed checks fail their criteria and stay accepted as blocking defects.\n\n**The CAN2 termination disagreement (circ-01 minor vs PHY-03 major) is resolved by evidence.** Both reviewers observed the same fact — the base board's 120 Ω terminators R36/R37 are DNP, so the board itself provides zero CAN2 termination. The physical reviewer rated this a major concern because the advertised internal wideband CAN link would fail with no termination anywhere. I independently re-verified the circuit reviewer's resolution: I re-fetched the upstream Polygonus module schematic (byte-identical, sha256 `8bc90db0…`), confirmed its R10 is a populated 120 Ω (`dnp no`), and traced its wires myself to the CANH2/CANL2 hierarchical labels. With a Polygonus brain module installed, the internal bus is single-terminated and functional, which defuses the major failure mechanism; what remains is a configuration-dependence concern (Atlas module unverifiable at a 404 URL, builder population choices). PHY-03 is therefore a duplicate of circ-01, which I keep as a **noted** concern — the \"n.p.\" annotation shows the DNP is deliberate, and no declared criterion (ERC/DRC/netlist/geometry) is violated.\n\n**Cross-reviewer duplicates consolidated.** The two reviewers independently confirmed the same three detailed defects, which I verified directly in the candidate: the five J1 connector peg holes saved as PTH pads with pad size equal to drill (PHY-01 canonical, circ-03 duplicate), the three starved thermal reliefs on GND pads C14/C15/U7 in the saved fill (PHY-02 canonical, circ-04 duplicate), and the five ERC errors rooted in missing PWR_FLAG/no-connect markers and symbol pin typing (circ-02 canonical, PHY-07 duplicate).\n\n**Other accepted defect.** PHY-06 (library tables): I confirmed from the candidate's own files that `fp-lib-table` omits the Simon footprint library even though `Simon.pretty` is in the repo, and no hellen-one-common library exists anywhere — with the J2 board-vs-symbol footprint substitution as a demonstrated consequence. Accepted as a minor reproducibility defect.\n\n**Noted concerns.** The byte-identical case-variant sheet alias (circ-05, matches a declared packet limitation), the MAX9924 input polarity swap (circ-06, netlist-supported but no requirement fixes polarity), and the two copper-marginality analyses (PHY-04 heater returns, PHY-05 ETB supply necks) whose arithmetic I spot-checked and reproduced — supported engineering concerns, but no declared current or thermal limit is violated.\n\nMy verification record is at `review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5257,"cache_read_input_tokens":333612,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5257},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"480c3efe-ca31-49ae-85c1-8e190ef2ac79","uuid":"89698efb-911d-4140-9f3b-4906e03220ad","timestamp":"2026-10-17T00:54:29.696Z","request_id":"req_011Cg6txDmYXC1axMNrfusK8"}
