review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md","locator":"section 4 - sha256 of both files and root Sheetfile reference"},{"path":"work/netlist/design.xml","locator":"sheet number 4 '/VR Conditioner/' source 'VR Conditioner.kicad_sch'"}]},{"finding_id":"circuit/circ-06-max9924-input-polarity","disposition":"noted","reason":"Supported info-level observation: the netlist confirms /CRANK + reaches U10.2 (IN-) via R25/R27 and /CRANK - reaches U10.1 (IN+) via R26/R28, inverted relative to the MAX9924 typical application. No declared requirement fixes the intended edge polarity, zero-cross detection is symmetric, and firmware edge selection can absorb a static inversion, so a defect is not established; preserved as a concern for human confirmation of the intended firmware pairing.","evidence":[{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"'/CRANK +': [J1.59,R25.2]; 'Net-(R25-Pad1)': [R25.1,R27.2]; 'Net-(U10-IN-)': [...,R27.1,...,U10.2]; '/CRANK -': [J1.55,R26.2]; 'Net-(U10-IN+)': [...,R28.1,...,U10.1]"},{"path":"review-work/circuit/experiments/notes.md","locator":"section 5 - MAX9924 wiring observation"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-01","disposition":"accepted","reason":"Established minor defect, canonical for the J1 padstack issue. Independently re-parsed the saved board: the Simon:Molex_112_643330100 footprint contains exactly five unnumbered no-net thru-hole pads with pad size equal to drill (4.0/4.0 mm x3, 2.2/2.2 mm x2), producing the 5 padstack and 5 annular_width DRC errors against the 0.1 mm minimum. Mechanical peg holes should be NPTH; as saved they request ringless plated barrels that fabricators flag or that risk plating tear-out. No net attached, so impact is manufacturing/mechanical only (minor).","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"violations[] type=padstack and type=annular_width, severity=error, items 'PTH pad [<no net>] of J1'"},{"path":"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md","locator":"section 3 - pad parse: 5 of 117 thru-hole pads with size==drill, positions match DRC"},{"path":"inputs/project/Polygonus-Universal-Base.kicad_pcb","locator":"footprint 'Simon:Molex_112_643330100' (J1 at 133.2,43.34), unnumbered thru_hole pads with size==drill"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-02","disposition":"accepted","reason":"Established minor defect, canonical for the starved thermals. The saved F.Cu GND fill connects pads C15.2, U7.4, and C14.2 with one thermal spoke where the zone's own constraint requires two; verified as the three error-severity starved_thermal entries in the full DRC report. Pads remain electrically connected (0 unconnected items), so the impact is joint robustness and connection impedance rather than function, but the board violates its own fill constraints as saved and the read-only review must take the fill as-is.","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"3x type=starved_thermal severity=error: Pad 2 [GND] of C15, Pad 4 [GND] of U7, Pad 2 [GND] of C14 on F.Cu"},{"path":"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md","locator":"section 1 - starved_thermal items and unconnected=0 re-verified"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-03","disposition":"duplicate","duplicate_of":"circuit/circ-01-can2-termination-dnp","reason":"Same observation as circuit/circ-01 (R36/R37 120R DNP leaves the base board's CAN2 bus with zero on-board termination). The major-severity mechanism - advertised internal wideband CAN failing for lack of any termination - is resolved by evidence: I independently re-fetched the Polygonus module source (byte-identical) and wire-traced its populated 120R R10 across CANH2/CANL2, so the documented primary configuration is single-terminated and functional. The residual exposure (unverifiable Atlas module, builder over/under-population) is exactly the configuration-dependence concern preserved as the noted canonical circ-01. Both findings are concerns (non-defects), so consolidation is permissible.","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md","locator":"section 2 - upstream sha256 match and independent BFS wire trace R10 pins -> CANH2/CANL2 labels"},{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"R36/R37 (dnp yes)(in_bom no) value 120; 'n.p.' annotation"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"footprint R36 dnp:true, pads on /CAN2+ and /CAN2-"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-04","disposition":"noted","reason":"Supported minor concern. I reproduced the arithmetic (0.6 mm x 35 um x 112 mm gives ~91 mOhm; IPC-2221 external 0.6 mm/1 oz ~1.65 A at 10 C rise; ~25-26 C rise at 2.5 A), and the segment extraction is documented in the physical experiments. The packet declares no current/thermal criterion and heater current is duty-limited by the module, so no defect is established; the single 0.6 mm heater-return traces are a legitimate marginality concern worth a width increase or documented justification.","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md","locator":"'Heater returns' section - segment listing, resistance and IPC-2221 estimates with assumptions"},{"path":"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md","locator":"section 6 - arithmetic spot-check reproducing R and ampacity figures"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets /HeaterNeg (J1.108,U1.11,U1.12) and /HeaterNeg2 (J1.76,U2.11,U2.12)"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-05","disposition":"noted","reason":"Supported minor concern. The extraction (0.8 mm F.Cu neck feeding U15 pad 4; three 0.4 mm vias serving the whole /12V_MR_FUSE net toward U3) is documented with stated IPC-2221 assumptions, and nominal throttle currents sit within estimated limits; only sustained stall/current-limit events exceed them, and the TLE9201's internal limit/shutdown makes such events transient. No declared current criterion exists, so no defect is established; preserved as a calculated marginality concern recommending wider necks or paralleled vias.","evidence":[{"path":"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md","locator":"'ETB H-bridge supply (/12V_MR_FUSE)' section - track/via/pad extraction and ampacity estimates"},{"path":"work/geometry/geometry.json","locator":"U15 pad 4 /12V_MR_FUSE SMD at (120.54,44.91); U3 pad 4 at (103.68,45.1)"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-06","disposition":"accepted","reason":"Established minor defect. Verified from the candidate's own files: fp-lib-table registers only wideband_module, header_placement and fome_modules while fome-kicad-libs/Simon.pretty exists unregistered in the project tree, and no hellen-one-common library file exists anywhere in the candidate (find returned nothing). This matches the native lib_symbol_issues/footprint_link_issues/lib_footprint_issues warnings, and the DRC parity report shows an actual consequence already present: board J2 carries Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD while the symbol specifies fome_modules:polygonus. A clean checkout cannot re-resolve or audit these footprints/symbols. No electrical impact in the saved state (caches intact), hence minor.","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/fp-lib-table","locator":"3 entries only; no 'Simon' footprint library despite ${KIPRJMOD}/fome-kicad-libs/Simon.pretty existing"},{"path":"inputs/project/sym-lib-table","locator":"Simon and fome_modules only; no hellen-one-common entry or file in project"},{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"schematic_parity: 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)' (J2); lib_footprint_issues for library 'Simon'"},{"path":"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md","locator":"section 5 - table contents and library-directory listing"}]},{"finding_id":"physical/PHY-07","disposition":"duplicate","duplicate_of":"circuit/circ-02-erc-errors","reason":"Same defect as circuit/circ-02: the identical five native ERC errors with the same root-cause attribution (missing PWR_FLAG on harness-fed rails, unmarked NC on A1 ~FLT, paralleled Power-output pins J2.40/41). Both reviewers independently confirmed the same items; consolidated under the circuit finding as canonical (defect-to-defect duplication, severity carried as minor by the canonical).","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"severity=error entries: power_pin_not_driven x3, pin_not_connected (A1 ~FLT), pin_to_pin (J2 40/41)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"/12V_KEY (J1.45,J2.90), /5V_SENSOR_1 (J2.40,J2.41), unconnected-(A1-~{FLT}-Pad2)"}]}]}}}
