al. The residual exposure (unverifiable Atlas module, builder over/under-population) is exactly the configuration-dependence concern preserved as the noted canonical circ-01. Both findings are concerns (non-defects), so consolidation is permissible.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md\",\"locator\":\"section 2 - upstream sha256 match and independent BFS wire trace R10 pins -> CANH2/CANL2 labels\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch\",\"locator\":\"R36/R37 (dnp yes)(in_bom no) value 120; 'n.p.' annotation\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"footprint R36 dnp:true, pads on /CAN2+ and /CAN2-\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-04\",\"disposition\":\"noted\",\"reason\":\"Supported minor concern. I reproduced the arithmetic (0.6 mm x 35 um x 112 mm gives ~91 mOhm; IPC-2221 external 0.6 mm/1 oz ~1.65 A at 10 C rise; ~25-26 C rise at 2.5 A), and the segment extraction is documented in the physical experiments. The packet declares no current/thermal criterion and heater current is duty-limited by the module, so no defect is established; the single 0.6 mm heater-return traces are a legitimate marginality concern worth a width increase or documented justification.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md\",\"locator\":\"'Heater returns' section - segment listing, resistance and IPC-2221 estimates with assumptions\"},{\"path\":\"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md\",\"locator\":\"section 6 - arithmetic spot-check reproducing R and ampacity figures\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"nets /HeaterNeg (J1.108,U1.11,U1.12) and /HeaterNeg2 (J1.76,U2.11,U2.12)\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-05\",\"disposition\":\"noted\",\"reason\":\"Supported minor concern. The extraction (0.8 mm F.Cu neck feeding U15 pad 4; three 0.4 mm vias serving the whole /12V_MR_FUSE net toward U3) is documented with stated IPC-2221 assumptions, and nominal throttle currents sit within estimated limits; only sustained stall/current-limit events exceed them, and the TLE9201's internal limit/shutdown makes such events transient. No declared current criterion exists, so no defect is established; preserved as a calculated marginality concern recommending wider necks or paralleled vias.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"review-work/physical/experiments/physical-review-notes.md\",\"locator\":\"'ETB H-bridge supply (/12V_MR_FUSE)' section - track/via/pad extraction and ampacity estimates\"},{\"path\":\"work/geometry/geometry.json\",\"locator\":\"U15 pad 4 /12V_MR_FUSE SMD at (120.54,44.91); U3 pad 4 at (103.68,45.1)\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-06\",\"disposition\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"Established minor defect. Verified from the candidate's own files: fp-lib-table registers only wideband_module, header_placement and fome_modules while fome-kicad-libs/Simon.pretty exists unregistered in the project tree, and no hellen-one-common library file exists anywhere in the candidate (find returned nothing). This matches the native lib_symbol_issues/footprint_link_issues/lib_footprint_issues warnings, and the DRC parity report shows an actual consequence already present: board J2 carries Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD while the symbol specifies fome_modules:polygonus. A clean checkout cannot re-resolve or audit these footprints/symbols. No electrical impact in the saved state (caches intact), hence minor.\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"inputs/project/fp-lib-table\",\"locator\":\"3 entries only; no 'Simon' footprint library despite ${KIPRJMOD}/fome-kicad-libs/Simon.pretty existing\"},{\"path\":\"inputs/project/sym-lib-table\",\"locator\":\"Simon and fome_modules only; no hellen-one-common entry or file in project\"},{\"path\":\"work/drc/drc.json\",\"locator\":\"schematic_parity: 'Simon:Polygonus-With-USB-SWD doesn't match footprint given by symbol (fome_modules:polygonus)' (J2); lib_footprint_issues for library 'Simon'\"},{\"path\":\"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md\",\"locator\":\"section 5 - table contents and library-directory listing\"}]},{\"finding_id\":\"physical/PHY-07\",\"disposition\":\"duplicate\",\"duplicate_of\":\"circuit/circ-02-erc-errors\",\"reason\":\"Same defect as circuit/circ-02: the identical five native ERC errors with the same root-cause attribution (missing PWR_FLAG on harness-fed rails, unmarked NC on A1 ~FLT, paralleled Power-output pins J2.40/41). Both reviewers independently confirmed the same items; consolidated under the circuit finding as canonical (defect-to-defect duplication, severity carried as minor by the canonical).\",\"evidence\":[{\"path\":\"work/erc/erc.json\",\"locator\":\"severity=error entries: power_pin_not_driven x3, pin_not_connected (A1 ~FLT), pin_to_pin (J2 40/41)\"},{\"path\":\"work/netlist/connectivity.json\",\"locator\":\"/12V_KEY (J1.45,J2.90), /5V_SENSOR_1 (J2.40,J2.41), unconnected-(A1-~{FLT}-Pad2)\"}]}]}","structured_output":{"candidate_id":"46e5a5c34e7b9715155c9e90277cd3639b3a19ebb9590053a081bbb6436ba860","run_id":"8534a2a6-e237-4d1c-a002-90ce37ec09e4","schema":"agent-ee.decisions/1","decisions":[{"finding_id":"check/erc","disposition":"accepted","reason":"Executed ERC check fails its criterion: 353 violations including 5 errors (3x power_pin_not_driven, 1x pin_not_connected, 1x pin_to_pin). Counts re-verified from the full evidence file and independently reproduced by the circuit reviewer's rerun. Failing check criterion must remain accepted; root-cause triage of the 5 errors is carried by circuit/circ-02.","evidence":[{"path":"work/erc/erc.json","locator":"353 violations; severity=error entries: power_pin_not_driven x3, pin_not_connected (A1 ~FLT), pin_to_pin (J2 40/41)"},{"path":"work/erc/console.log","locator":"Found 353 violations"},{"path":"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md","locator":"section 1 - error-count re-verification"}]},{"finding_id":"check/drc","disposition":"accepted","reason":"Executed DRC check fails its criterion: 142 violations including 13 errors (5 padstack, 5 annular_width, 3 starved_thermal), 114 schematic-parity issues, 0 unconnected items. Re-verified from the full evidence file and reproduced by both reviewers. The error-level items are detailed in accepted findings physical/PHY-01 and physical/PHY-02.","evidence":[{"path":"work/drc/drc.json","locator":"error types: padstack x5, annular_width x5, starved_thermal x3; 114 schematic_parity entries; unconnected_items empty"},{"path":"work/drc/console.log","locator":"Found 142 violations / 0 unconnected / 114 parity"},{"path":"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md","locator":"section 1 - error-count re-verification"}]},{"finding_id":"circuit/circ-01-can2-termination-dnp","disposition":"noted","reason":"Supported configuration-dependence concern, canonical for the CAN2 termination topic. Verified: base-board terminators R36/R37 (120R) are DNP with an explicit 'n.p.' annotation, so the board alone provides no CAN2 termination; I independently re-fetched the Polygonus module source (byte-identical sha256 8bc90db0...) and wire-traced its populated 120R R10 (dnp no) across CANH2/CANL2, confirming the documented primary configuration is single-terminated and functional. Residual exposure is limited to unverifiable Atlas-module compatibility (repo 404) and builder population choices. The DNP is deliberate and violates no declared criterion, so this is a minor concern, not a defect.","evidence":[{"path":"inputs/project/wbo-can-trans.kicad_sch","locator":"symbol uuid d69380f9-5487-4782-9ce9-0690df62e543 R36/R37 value 120 (dnp yes)(in_bom no); text 'n.p.' at (113.03,76.2)"},{"path":"work/netlist/connectivity.json","locator":"nets /CAN2+ and /CAN2- node lists; dnp_refs include R36,R37"},{"path":"review-work/adjudicator/experiments/adjudication-notes.md","locator":"section 2 - independent re-fetch and wire-graph trace of Polygonus R10 to CANH